# Round 156: three defaults that put a boxed value into a numeric slot.
#  (1) a value-called function's parameter counted "passed to a builtin"
#      as numeric evidence: `send of [c, x * y]` kept the channel `c`
#      numeric (corpus test_spawn_args);
#  (2) the call-site argument classifier answered "unknown" for any call
#      not in BOXED_RET_BUILTINS -- an unlisted builtin (try_recv -> null),
#      an imported name, a value or module-qualified callee -- so the
#      callee's numeric parameter was never widened (test_channel_nb,
#      test_meta_parity, test_observer_slots);
#  (3) a module-assigned name with positive BOXED evidence (`msg is "hi"`)
#      passed to a numeric parameter widened nothing. (A module name of
#      UNKNOWN class -- `ch is channel of 1` -- still keeps the checked
#      unbox at the call site, loud when wrong: boxing every unknown
#      module name cost DMG 5.7%; #202.)
# Each exited "non-numeric value in a numeric context ..." rc 1 where the
# VM runs (rc 0). Evidence now: a numbers-only use, `+` with a numeric
# operand, or a compiled callee's numeric position; everything else boxed.
define producer(c, x, y) as:
    send of [c, x * y]
define shout(m) as:
    return m
define twice(n) as:
    return n * 2
define via(c, n) as:
    send of [c, twice of n]
define check(name, got, want) as:
    if got == want:
        print of ("ok " + name)
    else:
        print of ("FAIL " + name)
define offset_of(base, off) as:
    return (base * 4) + off
ch is channel of 1
t is spawn of [producer, ch, 6, 7]
thread_join of t
print of (recv of ch)
msg is "hi"
print of (shout of msg)
t2 is spawn of [via, ch, 5]
thread_join of t2
print of (recv of ch)
check of ["empty", try_recv of ch, null]
check of ["str", str of 42, "42"]
check of ["num", 1 + 1, 2]
print of (offset_of of [3, 5])
